This dataset contains raw data from an fMRI study investigating whether the human brain represents affective space using grid-like codes.

During scanning, participants viewed emotion-laden stimuli presented in two modalities: morphs of facial expressions and sequences of phrases. Each trial consisted of a trajectory between two points in a two-dimensional affective space defined by valence and arousal. Participants judged whether the valence or arousal of the presented stimuli increased, decreased, or remained the same.

Behavioral data: https://osf.io/5fkuy/

Analysis code: https://github.com/ecco-laboratory/EmotionConceptNavigation